{"question_id":"1lsgy7zzo","content":"<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p>Statement (I) : The orbitals having same energy are called as degenerate orbitals.</p>\n<p>Statement (II) : In hydrogen atom, 3p and 3d orbitals are not degenerate orbitals.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>","chapter":"structure-of-atom","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-30th-january-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 30th January Morning Shift","permalink":"pgiven-below-are-two-statements-p-pstatement-i--t-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-w3o3q5ifkmn02ssl","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p>Statement (I) : The orbitals having same energy are called as degenerate orbitals.</p>\n<p>Statement (II) : In hydrogen atom, 3p and 3d orbitals are not degenerate orbitals.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement I is true but Statement II is false\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is false but Statement II is true\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p><strong>Degenerate Orbitals</strong>: Orbitals that have the same energy are called degenerate orbitals.  </p>\n<p><p><strong>Hydrogen-like Atoms (Single-Electron Systems)</strong>: In a hydrogen atom (or any one-electron system), the energy of an orbital depends <strong>only</strong> on the principal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, <em>not</em> on the azimuthal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. Therefore, all orbitals with the same <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (e.g., 3s, 3p, 3d) have the same energy and are <strong>degenerate</strong>.  </p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Multi-electron Atoms</strong>: In atoms with more than one electron, the energy also depends on <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (and other factors like screening), so 3s, 3p, and 3d orbitals are <strong>not</strong> all degenerate in multi-electron atoms.</p></p>\n\n<p>Now, let us evaluate the given statements:</p>\n\n<p><p><strong>Statement (I)</strong>: \u201cThe orbitals having same energy are called as degenerate orbitals.\u201d  </p>\n<p>This statement is <strong>true</strong> by definition.</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Statement (II)</strong>: \u201cIn hydrogen atom, 3p and 3d orbitals are not degenerate orbitals.\u201d  </p>\n<p>In a hydrogen atom, all orbitals with the same principal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (like 3s, 3p, 3d) <strong>are</strong> degenerate.  </p>\n<p>Hence, this statement is <strong>false</strong>.</p></p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct option is:</p>\n<p><strong>Option A: Statement I is true but Statement II is false.</strong></p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>\u0928\u0940\u091a\u0947 \u0926\u094b \u0915\u0925\u0928 \u0926\u093f\u090f \u0917\u090f \u0939\u0948\u0902 :</p>\n<p>\u0915\u0925\u0928 (I) : \u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928 \u0909\u0930\u094d\u091c\u093e \u0935\u093e\u0932\u0947 \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u094b \u0921\u093f\u091c\u0947\u0928\u0947\u0930\u0947\u091f \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0915\u0939\u093e \u091c\u093e\u0924\u093e \u0939\u0948\u0964</p>\n<p>\u0915\u0925\u0928 (II) : \u0939\u093e\u0907\u0921\u094d\u0930\u094b\u091c\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941 \u092e\u0947\u0902 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.389ex\" height=\"1.943ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 1056 859\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u090f\u0935\u0902 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.452ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.747ex\" height=\"2.149ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 1656 950\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">\u00a0</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"64\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-64\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0921\u093f\u091c\u0947\u0928\u0947\u0930\u0947\u091f \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0928\u0939\u0940\u0902 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964</p>\n<p>\u0909\u092a\u0930\u094d\u092f\u0941\u0915\u094d\u0924 \u0915\u0925\u0928\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u0947 \u0938\u0902\u0926\u0930\u094d\u092d \u092e\u0947\u0902, \u0928\u0940\u091a\u0947 \u0926\u093f\u090f \u0917\u090f \u0935\u093f\u0915\u0932\u094d\u092a\u094b\u0902 \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0938\u0947 \u0938\u0930\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0927\u093f\u0915 \u0909\u092a\u092f\u0941\u0915\u094d\u0924 \u0909\u0924\u094d\u0924\u0930 \u091a\u0941\u0928\u0947 :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"\u0915\u0925\u0928 I \u0938\u0939\u0940 \u0939\u0948 \u092a\u0930\u0902\u0924\u0941 \u0915\u0925\u0928 II \u0917\u0932\u0924 \u0939\u0948\u0964\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"\u0915\u0925\u0928 I \u0917\u0932\u0924 \u0939\u0948 \u092a\u0930\u0902\u0924\u0941 \u0915\u0925\u0928 II \u0938\u0939\u0940 \u0939\u0948\u0964\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"\u0926\u094b\u0928\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u0925\u0928 I \u090f\u0935\u0902 \u0915\u0925\u0928 II \u0917\u0932\u0924 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"\u0926\u094b\u0928\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u0925\u0928 I \u090f\u0935\u0902 \u0915\u0925\u0928 II \u0938\u0939\u0940 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p><strong>\u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915</strong>: \u091c\u093f\u0928 \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u0940 \u090a\u0930\u094d\u091c\u093e \u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928 \u0939\u094b\u0924\u0940 \u0939\u0948, \u0909\u0928\u094d\u0939\u0947\u0902 \u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0915\u0939\u0924\u0947 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964</p>\n<p><p><strong>\u0939\u093e\u0907\u0921\u094d\u0930\u094b\u091c\u0928-\u0938\u0926\u0943\u0936 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941 (\u090f\u0915\u0932-\u0907\u0932\u0947\u0915\u094d\u091f\u094d\u0930\u0949\u0928 \u0928\u093f\u0915\u093e\u092f)</strong>: \u0939\u093e\u0907\u0921\u094d\u0930\u094b\u091c\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941 (\u092f\u093e \u0915\u093f\u0938\u0940 \u090f\u0915-\u0907\u0932\u0947\u0915\u094d\u091f\u094d\u0930\u0949\u0928 \u0928\u093f\u0915\u093e\u092f) \u092e\u0947\u0902, \u0915\u093f\u0938\u0940 \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0915\u0940 \u090a\u0930\u094d\u091c\u093e <strong>\u0915\u0947\u0935\u0932</strong> \u092e\u0941\u0916\u094d\u092f \u0915\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0902\u091f\u092e \u0938\u0902\u0916\u094d\u092f\u093e <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u092a\u0930 \u0928\u093f\u0930\u094d\u092d\u0930 \u0915\u0930\u0924\u0940 \u0939\u0948, \u0926\u093f\u0917\u0902\u0936\u0940 \u0915\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0902\u091f\u092e \u0938\u0902\u0916\u094d\u092f\u093e <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u092a\u0930 <em>\u0928\u0939\u0940\u0902</em>\u0964 \u0907\u0938\u0932\u093f\u090f, \u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u0935\u093e\u0932\u0947 \u0938\u092d\u0940 \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 (\u091c\u0948\u0938\u0947, 3s, 3p, 3d) \u0915\u0940 \u090a\u0930\u094d\u091c\u093e \u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928 \u0939\u094b\u0924\u0940 \u0939\u0948 \u0914\u0930 \u0935\u0947 <strong>\u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f</strong> \u0939\u094b\u0924\u0947 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>\u092c\u0939\u0941-\u0907\u0932\u0947\u0915\u094d\u091f\u094d\u0930\u0949\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941</strong>: \u090f\u0915 \u0938\u0947 \u0905\u0927\u093f\u0915 \u0907\u0932\u0947\u0915\u094d\u091f\u094d\u0930\u0949\u0928 \u0935\u093e\u0932\u0947 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941\u0913\u0902 \u092e\u0947\u0902, \u090a\u0930\u094d\u091c\u093e <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u092a\u0930 \u092d\u0940 \u0928\u093f\u0930\u094d\u092d\u0930 \u0915\u0930\u0924\u0940 \u0939\u0948 (\u0914\u0930 \u092a\u0930\u093f\u0930\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0923 \u091c\u0948\u0938\u0947 \u0905\u0928\u094d\u092f \u0915\u093e\u0930\u0915\u094b\u0902 \u092a\u0930), \u0907\u0938\u0932\u093f\u090f \u092c\u0939\u0941-\u0907\u0932\u0947\u0915\u094d\u091f\u094d\u0930\u0949\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941\u0913\u0902 \u092e\u0947\u0902 3s, 3p, \u0914\u0930 3d \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0938\u092d\u0940 \u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f <strong>\u0928\u0939\u0940\u0902</strong> \u0939\u094b\u0924\u0947 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964</p></p>\n\n<p>\u0905\u092c, \u0906\u0907\u090f \u0926\u093f\u090f \u0917\u090f \u0915\u0925\u0928\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u093e \u092e\u0942\u0932\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0902\u0915\u0928 \u0915\u0930\u0947\u0902:</p>\n\n<p><p><strong>\u0915\u0925\u0928 (I)</strong>: \"\u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928 \u090a\u0930\u094d\u091c\u093e \u0935\u093e\u0932\u0947 \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u094b \u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0915\u0939\u093e \u091c\u093e\u0924\u093e \u0939\u0948\u0964\"</p>\n<p>\u092f\u0939 \u0915\u0925\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u093f\u092d\u093e\u0937\u093e \u0915\u0947 \u0905\u0928\u0941\u0938\u093e\u0930 <strong>\u0938\u0924\u094d\u092f</strong> \u0939\u0948\u0964</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>\u0915\u0925\u0928 (II)</strong>: \"\u0939\u093e\u0907\u0921\u094d\u0930\u094b\u091c\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941 \u092e\u0947\u0902, 3p \u0914\u0930 3d \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0928\u0939\u0940\u0902 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964\"</p>\n<p>\u0939\u093e\u0907\u0921\u094d\u0930\u094b\u091c\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941 \u092e\u0947\u0902, \u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928 \u092e\u0941\u0916\u094d\u092f \u0915\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0902\u091f\u092e \u0938\u0902\u0916\u094d\u092f\u093e <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u0935\u093e\u0932\u0947 \u0938\u092d\u0940 \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 (\u091c\u0948\u0938\u0947 3s, 3p, 3d) <strong>\u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f \u0939\u094b\u0924\u0947 \u0939\u0948\u0902</strong>\u0964</p>\n<p>\u0905\u0924\u0903, \u092f\u0939 \u0915\u0925\u0928 <strong>\u0905\u0938\u0924\u094d\u092f</strong> \u0939\u0948\u0964</p></p>\n\n<p>\u0907\u0938\u0932\u093f\u090f, \u0938\u0939\u0940 \u0935\u093f\u0915\u0932\u094d\u092a \u0939\u0948:</p>\n<p><strong>\u0935\u093f\u0915\u0932\u094d\u092a A: \u0915\u0925\u0928 I \u0938\u0924\u094d\u092f \u0939\u0948 \u0932\u0947\u0915\u093f\u0928 \u0915\u0925\u0928 II \u0905\u0938\u0924\u094d\u092f \u0939\u0948\u0964</strong></p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"quantum-numbers-and-orbitals","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["assertion_reason"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-30th-january-morning-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement I is true but Statement II is false\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is false but Statement II is true\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p><strong>Degenerate Orbitals</strong>: Orbitals that have the same energy are called degenerate orbitals.  </p>\n<p><p><strong>Hydrogen-like Atoms (Single-Electron Systems)</strong>: In a hydrogen atom (or any one-electron system), the energy of an orbital depends <strong>only</strong> on the principal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, <em>not</em> on the azimuthal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. Therefore, all orbitals with the same <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (e.g., 3s, 3p, 3d) have the same energy and are <strong>degenerate</strong>.  </p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Multi-electron Atoms</strong>: In atoms with more than one electron, the energy also depends on <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (and other factors like screening), so 3s, 3p, and 3d orbitals are <strong>not</strong> all degenerate in multi-electron atoms.</p></p>\n\n<p>Now, let us evaluate the given statements:</p>\n\n<p><p><strong>Statement (I)</strong>: \u201cThe orbitals having same energy are called as degenerate orbitals.\u201d  </p>\n<p>This statement is <strong>true</strong> by definition.</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Statement (II)</strong>: \u201cIn hydrogen atom, 3p and 3d orbitals are not degenerate orbitals.\u201d  </p>\n<p>In a hydrogen atom, all orbitals with the same principal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (like 3s, 3p, 3d) <strong>are</strong> degenerate.  </p>\n<p>Hence, this statement is <strong>false</strong>.</p></p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct option is:</p>\n<p><strong>Option A: Statement I is true but Statement II is false.</strong></p>","qKey":"pgiven-below-are-two-statements-p-pstatement-i--t-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-w3o3q5ifkmn02ssl","paperKey":"jee-main-2024-online-30th-january-morning-shift","questions":[{"question_id":"1lsgy7zzo","content":"<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p>Statement (I) : The orbitals having same energy are called as degenerate orbitals.</p>\n<p>Statement (II) : In hydrogen atom, 3p and 3d orbitals are not degenerate orbitals.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>","chapter":"structure-of-atom","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-30th-january-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 30th January Morning Shift","permalink":"pgiven-below-are-two-statements-p-pstatement-i--t-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-w3o3q5ifkmn02ssl","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>Given below are two statements :</p>\n<p>Statement (I) : The orbitals having same energy are called as degenerate orbitals.</p>\n<p>Statement (II) : In hydrogen atom, 3p and 3d orbitals are not degenerate orbitals.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement I is true but Statement II is false\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is false but Statement II is true\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p><strong>Degenerate Orbitals</strong>: Orbitals that have the same energy are called degenerate orbitals.  </p>\n<p><p><strong>Hydrogen-like Atoms (Single-Electron Systems)</strong>: In a hydrogen atom (or any one-electron system), the energy of an orbital depends <strong>only</strong> on the principal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, <em>not</em> on the azimuthal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. Therefore, all orbitals with the same <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (e.g., 3s, 3p, 3d) have the same energy and are <strong>degenerate</strong>.  </p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Multi-electron Atoms</strong>: In atoms with more than one electron, the energy also depends on <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (and other factors like screening), so 3s, 3p, and 3d orbitals are <strong>not</strong> all degenerate in multi-electron atoms.</p></p>\n\n<p>Now, let us evaluate the given statements:</p>\n\n<p><p><strong>Statement (I)</strong>: \u201cThe orbitals having same energy are called as degenerate orbitals.\u201d  </p>\n<p>This statement is <strong>true</strong> by definition.</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Statement (II)</strong>: \u201cIn hydrogen atom, 3p and 3d orbitals are not degenerate orbitals.\u201d  </p>\n<p>In a hydrogen atom, all orbitals with the same principal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (like 3s, 3p, 3d) <strong>are</strong> degenerate.  </p>\n<p>Hence, this statement is <strong>false</strong>.</p></p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct option is:</p>\n<p><strong>Option A: Statement I is true but Statement II is false.</strong></p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"comprehension":null,"content":"<p>\u0928\u0940\u091a\u0947 \u0926\u094b \u0915\u0925\u0928 \u0926\u093f\u090f \u0917\u090f \u0939\u0948\u0902 :</p>\n<p>\u0915\u0925\u0928 (I) : \u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928 \u0909\u0930\u094d\u091c\u093e \u0935\u093e\u0932\u0947 \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u094b \u0921\u093f\u091c\u0947\u0928\u0947\u0930\u0947\u091f \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0915\u0939\u093e \u091c\u093e\u0924\u093e \u0939\u0948\u0964</p>\n<p>\u0915\u0925\u0928 (II) : \u0939\u093e\u0907\u0921\u094d\u0930\u094b\u091c\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941 \u092e\u0947\u0902 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.389ex\" height=\"1.943ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -665 1056 859\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u090f\u0935\u0902 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.452ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.747ex\" height=\"2.149ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 1656 950\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">\u00a0</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"64\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-64\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0921\u093f\u091c\u0947\u0928\u0947\u0930\u0947\u091f \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0928\u0939\u0940\u0902 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964</p>\n<p>\u0909\u092a\u0930\u094d\u092f\u0941\u0915\u094d\u0924 \u0915\u0925\u0928\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u0947 \u0938\u0902\u0926\u0930\u094d\u092d \u092e\u0947\u0902, \u0928\u0940\u091a\u0947 \u0926\u093f\u090f \u0917\u090f \u0935\u093f\u0915\u0932\u094d\u092a\u094b\u0902 \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0938\u0947 \u0938\u0930\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0927\u093f\u0915 \u0909\u092a\u092f\u0941\u0915\u094d\u0924 \u0909\u0924\u094d\u0924\u0930 \u091a\u0941\u0928\u0947 :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"\u0915\u0925\u0928 I \u0938\u0939\u0940 \u0939\u0948 \u092a\u0930\u0902\u0924\u0941 \u0915\u0925\u0928 II \u0917\u0932\u0924 \u0939\u0948\u0964\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"\u0915\u0925\u0928 I \u0917\u0932\u0924 \u0939\u0948 \u092a\u0930\u0902\u0924\u0941 \u0915\u0925\u0928 II \u0938\u0939\u0940 \u0939\u0948\u0964\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"\u0926\u094b\u0928\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u0925\u0928 I \u090f\u0935\u0902 \u0915\u0925\u0928 II \u0917\u0932\u0924 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"\u0926\u094b\u0928\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u0925\u0928 I \u090f\u0935\u0902 \u0915\u0925\u0928 II \u0938\u0939\u0940 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p><strong>\u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915</strong>: \u091c\u093f\u0928 \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u0940 \u090a\u0930\u094d\u091c\u093e \u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928 \u0939\u094b\u0924\u0940 \u0939\u0948, \u0909\u0928\u094d\u0939\u0947\u0902 \u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0915\u0939\u0924\u0947 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964</p>\n<p><p><strong>\u0939\u093e\u0907\u0921\u094d\u0930\u094b\u091c\u0928-\u0938\u0926\u0943\u0936 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941 (\u090f\u0915\u0932-\u0907\u0932\u0947\u0915\u094d\u091f\u094d\u0930\u0949\u0928 \u0928\u093f\u0915\u093e\u092f)</strong>: \u0939\u093e\u0907\u0921\u094d\u0930\u094b\u091c\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941 (\u092f\u093e \u0915\u093f\u0938\u0940 \u090f\u0915-\u0907\u0932\u0947\u0915\u094d\u091f\u094d\u0930\u0949\u0928 \u0928\u093f\u0915\u093e\u092f) \u092e\u0947\u0902, \u0915\u093f\u0938\u0940 \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0915\u0940 \u090a\u0930\u094d\u091c\u093e <strong>\u0915\u0947\u0935\u0932</strong> \u092e\u0941\u0916\u094d\u092f \u0915\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0902\u091f\u092e \u0938\u0902\u0916\u094d\u092f\u093e <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u092a\u0930 \u0928\u093f\u0930\u094d\u092d\u0930 \u0915\u0930\u0924\u0940 \u0939\u0948, \u0926\u093f\u0917\u0902\u0936\u0940 \u0915\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0902\u091f\u092e \u0938\u0902\u0916\u094d\u092f\u093e <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u092a\u0930 <em>\u0928\u0939\u0940\u0902</em>\u0964 \u0907\u0938\u0932\u093f\u090f, \u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u0935\u093e\u0932\u0947 \u0938\u092d\u0940 \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 (\u091c\u0948\u0938\u0947, 3s, 3p, 3d) \u0915\u0940 \u090a\u0930\u094d\u091c\u093e \u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928 \u0939\u094b\u0924\u0940 \u0939\u0948 \u0914\u0930 \u0935\u0947 <strong>\u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f</strong> \u0939\u094b\u0924\u0947 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>\u092c\u0939\u0941-\u0907\u0932\u0947\u0915\u094d\u091f\u094d\u0930\u0949\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941</strong>: \u090f\u0915 \u0938\u0947 \u0905\u0927\u093f\u0915 \u0907\u0932\u0947\u0915\u094d\u091f\u094d\u0930\u0949\u0928 \u0935\u093e\u0932\u0947 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941\u0913\u0902 \u092e\u0947\u0902, \u090a\u0930\u094d\u091c\u093e <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u092a\u0930 \u092d\u0940 \u0928\u093f\u0930\u094d\u092d\u0930 \u0915\u0930\u0924\u0940 \u0939\u0948 (\u0914\u0930 \u092a\u0930\u093f\u0930\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0923 \u091c\u0948\u0938\u0947 \u0905\u0928\u094d\u092f \u0915\u093e\u0930\u0915\u094b\u0902 \u092a\u0930), \u0907\u0938\u0932\u093f\u090f \u092c\u0939\u0941-\u0907\u0932\u0947\u0915\u094d\u091f\u094d\u0930\u0949\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941\u0913\u0902 \u092e\u0947\u0902 3s, 3p, \u0914\u0930 3d \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0938\u092d\u0940 \u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f <strong>\u0928\u0939\u0940\u0902</strong> \u0939\u094b\u0924\u0947 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964</p></p>\n\n<p>\u0905\u092c, \u0906\u0907\u090f \u0926\u093f\u090f \u0917\u090f \u0915\u0925\u0928\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u093e \u092e\u0942\u0932\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0902\u0915\u0928 \u0915\u0930\u0947\u0902:</p>\n\n<p><p><strong>\u0915\u0925\u0928 (I)</strong>: \"\u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928 \u090a\u0930\u094d\u091c\u093e \u0935\u093e\u0932\u0947 \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u094b \u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0915\u0939\u093e \u091c\u093e\u0924\u093e \u0939\u0948\u0964\"</p>\n<p>\u092f\u0939 \u0915\u0925\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u093f\u092d\u093e\u0937\u093e \u0915\u0947 \u0905\u0928\u0941\u0938\u093e\u0930 <strong>\u0938\u0924\u094d\u092f</strong> \u0939\u0948\u0964</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>\u0915\u0925\u0928 (II)</strong>: \"\u0939\u093e\u0907\u0921\u094d\u0930\u094b\u091c\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941 \u092e\u0947\u0902, 3p \u0914\u0930 3d \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 \u0928\u0939\u0940\u0902 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964\"</p>\n<p>\u0939\u093e\u0907\u0921\u094d\u0930\u094b\u091c\u0928 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u0941 \u092e\u0947\u0902, \u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928 \u092e\u0941\u0916\u094d\u092f \u0915\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0902\u091f\u092e \u0938\u0902\u0916\u094d\u092f\u093e <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u0935\u093e\u0932\u0947 \u0938\u092d\u0940 \u0915\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0915 (\u091c\u0948\u0938\u0947 3s, 3p, 3d) <strong>\u0905\u092a\u092d\u094d\u0930\u0937\u094d\u091f \u0939\u094b\u0924\u0947 \u0939\u0948\u0902</strong>\u0964</p>\n<p>\u0905\u0924\u0903, \u092f\u0939 \u0915\u0925\u0928 <strong>\u0905\u0938\u0924\u094d\u092f</strong> \u0939\u0948\u0964</p></p>\n\n<p>\u0907\u0938\u0932\u093f\u090f, \u0938\u0939\u0940 \u0935\u093f\u0915\u0932\u094d\u092a \u0939\u0948:</p>\n<p><strong>\u0935\u093f\u0915\u0932\u094d\u092a A: \u0915\u0925\u0928 I \u0938\u0924\u094d\u092f \u0939\u0948 \u0932\u0947\u0915\u093f\u0928 \u0915\u0925\u0928 II \u0905\u0938\u0924\u094d\u092f \u0939\u0948\u0964</strong></p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"quantum-numbers-and-orbitals","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["assertion_reason"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-30th-january-morning-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement I is true but Statement II is false\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is false but Statement II is true\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p><strong>Degenerate Orbitals</strong>: Orbitals that have the same energy are called degenerate orbitals.  </p>\n<p><p><strong>Hydrogen-like Atoms (Single-Electron Systems)</strong>: In a hydrogen atom (or any one-electron system), the energy of an orbital depends <strong>only</strong> on the principal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, <em>not</em> on the azimuthal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. Therefore, all orbitals with the same <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (e.g., 3s, 3p, 3d) have the same energy and are <strong>degenerate</strong>.  </p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Multi-electron Atoms</strong>: In atoms with more than one electron, the energy also depends on <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.674ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 298 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D459\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D459\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (and other factors like screening), so 3s, 3p, and 3d orbitals are <strong>not</strong> all degenerate in multi-electron atoms.</p></p>\n\n<p>Now, let us evaluate the given statements:</p>\n\n<p><p><strong>Statement (I)</strong>: \u201cThe orbitals having same energy are called as degenerate orbitals.\u201d  </p>\n<p>This statement is <strong>true</strong> by definition.</p></p>\n<p><p><strong>Statement (II)</strong>: \u201cIn hydrogen atom, 3p and 3d orbitals are not degenerate orbitals.\u201d  </p>\n<p>In a hydrogen atom, all orbitals with the same principal quantum number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (like 3s, 3p, 3d) <strong>are</strong> degenerate.  </p>\n<p>Hence, this statement is <strong>false</strong>.</p></p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct option is:</p>\n<p><strong>Option A: Statement I is true but Statement II is false.</strong></p>","qKey":"pgiven-below-are-two-statements-p-pstatement-i--t-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-w3o3q5ifkmn02ssl","paperKey":"jee-main-2024-online-30th-january-morning-shift"}]}